REGULATION OF JOMBANG REGENCY

THE IMPLEMENTATION OF PROTECTION FOR CHILDREN VICTIMS OF VIOLENCE

CONCERNING

WOMEN

CHAPTER I

GENERAL PROVISIONS

Article 1

In this Regional Regulation, what is meant by:

1. Region is Jombang Regency;
2. Regional Government is the Regent and regional apparatus as elements of regional government administration;
3. Regent is the Regent of Jombang;
4. Regional House of Representatives hereinafter referred to as DPRD is the regional people's representative institution as an element of regional government administration;
5. Regional Government is the administration of government affairs by the Regional Government and DPRD according to the principles of Autonomy and assistance tasks with the principle of the Unitary State of the Republic of Indonesia as referred to in the 1945 Constitution of the Republic of Indonesia;
6. Agency is a Regional Work Unit whose main tasks and functions include the fields of social affairs, women's empowerment and child protection;
7. Child is a person who has not reached 18 years of age, including those in the womb;
8. Violence is any act that results in or may result in misery or suffering to the victim;
9. Physical violence is any act that causes pain, injury, wounds or disability to a person's body, miscarriage, unconsciousness and/or causes death;
10. Psychological violence is an act that causes fear, loss of self-confidence, loss of ability to act, feelings of helplessness and/or severe psychological suffering to a person:
11. Sexual violence is any act in the form of sexual harassment, coercion of sexual relations in an unnatural or unwanted manner against another person whether for commercial purposes and/or certain purposes;
12. Victim is a Woman and Child who experiences misery and or suffering as a result of violence;
13. Protection is all efforts aimed at providing a sense of security to victims either temporarily or based on a Court decision;
14. Service is an action that must be immediately taken to the victim when seeing, hearing and reasonably suspected that violence against the victim will, is or has occurred; 15. Companion is a person or representative of an institution who has the expertise to accompany victims to conduct counseling, therapy and advocacy for the strengthening and recovery of victims of violence;
16. Integrated Service Center for the Protection of Women and Children hereinafter referred to as P2T-P2A is a service provider institution based in a Hospital for victims of violence, especially women and children, which is managed jointly by the regional government and the community incorporated in a Team carried out in a cross-functional and cross-sectoral manner in the form of medical services (including medico-legal), psycho-social and legal services;
17. Safe house is a temporary residence used to provide protection to victims; 18. Community is individuals, families, groups, communities and social organizations;
19. Family is the smallest unit in society consisting of husband and wife, or husband, wife and their children, or father and his children, and mother and her children;

CHAPTER IV

OBLIGATIONS AND RESPONSIBILITIES

Article 6

1. The Regional Government is obliged and responsible to carry out efforts to prevent violence against women and children in the form of:a. conducting socialization regarding laws and regulations related to the implementation of protection for women and children victims of violence as well as anti-violence values against women and children; b. conducting monitoring and evaluation of the implementation of socialization and understanding of anti-violence values. (2) The Regional Government is obliged and responsible to carry out protection efforts for victims in the form of:a. collecting data and information about victims;
b. establishing and facilitating integrated service institutions and safe houses for victims;
c. encouraging public awareness of the importance of protection for victims;
3. The implementation of obligations as referred to in paragraph (1) and paragraph (2), is technically carried out in an integrated manner by the relevant Regional Work Units.

CHAPTER II

PRINCIPLES AND OBJECTIVES

Article 2

The principles of implementing protection for women and children victims of violence are:

1. Respect for the rights of victims;
2. Justice and gender equality;
3. Non-discrimination;
4. Best interests of the victim.

Article 9

Paragraph (1) What is meant by fast, safe, empathetic, non-discriminatory, easily accessible and with guaranteed confidentiality in the handling/examination of women and children victims of violence, victims are examined at the Secretariat of P2T-P2A or the Women and Children Protection Unit (UPPA) Room, which is a special closed and comfortable room at the Police Unit, where women and children victims of domestic violence and violence or sexual harassment can report their cases safely to policewomen who are empathetic, understanding and professional.

Paragraph (2) What is meant by no fees charged is that there is an exemption from visum fees free of charge for women and children victims of physical and sexual violence which can be done at the Regional General Hospital of Jombang Regency as well as at the Community Health Center (PUSKESMAS) with a visum letter from the Police, which is further stipulated in the Technical Guidelines Book;

